e6ec827716083e928f5406d/comments","author":{"login":"DanielEScherzer","id":179652704,"node_id":"U_kgDOCrVIYA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/179652704?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielEScherzer","html_url":"https://github.com/DanielEScherzer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielEScherzer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielEScherzer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielEScherzer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielEScherzer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielEScherzer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielEScherzer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielEScherzer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielEScherzer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielEScherzer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"DanielEScherzer","id":179652704,"node_id":"U_kgDOCrVIYA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/179652704?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielEScherzer","html_url":"https://github.com/DanielEScherzer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielEScherzer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielEScherzer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielEScherzer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielEScherzer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielEScherzer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielEScherzer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielEScherzer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielEScherzer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielEScherzer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"6bfe63761f3370b2d9337368537a5b969f27c300","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/commits/6bfe63761f3370b2d9337368537a5b969f27c300","html_url":"https://github.com/php/php-src/commit/6bfe63761f3370b2d9337368537a5b969f27c300"}]},{"sha":"7e86f2c443382b2f03a546b51ca065872454c087","node_id":"C_kwDOAB0LotoAKDdlODZmMmM0NDMzODJiMmYwM2E1NDZiNTFjYTA2NTg3MjQ1NGMwODc","commit":{"author":{"name":"Jakub Zelenka","email":"bukka@php.net","date":"2026-11-01T16:22:19Z"},"committer":{"name":"Jakub Zelenka","email":"bukka@php.net","date":"2026-11-01T20:32:18Z"},"message":"openssl: Fix use-after-free in TLS session remove callback\n\nThe session remove callback reads the listener stream from the SSL_CTX\nex_data, but the context is shared with accepted connections and can\noutlive the listener. Closing the listener left a dangling pointer that\nthe callback later dereferenced. Clear it on close when it refers to the\nstream being freed.\n\nThe added test reproduces it via a TCP proxy and crashes under ASan\nwithout the fix.\n\nCloses GH-25132","tree":{"sha":"b6c023934d1d9c61dd5a1abb6bf3fb213015d66e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/git/trees/b6c023934d1d9c61dd5a1abb6bf3fb213015d66e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/git/commits/7e86f2c443382b2f03a546b51ca065872454c087","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQTCjZN1dWA+tKu3JYYcB3ncXAqd5AUCaueh0gAKCRAcB3ncXAqd\n5D0AAP9wvIJxHjwyfM9ltGtFyDjhT6dSB8HhNHaDb3qv7cjsiQEAka5sB1XsND4j\n+EliTw3QiKny41e9XMwrodKIdYoeVAg=\n=IYd+\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","payload":"tree b6c023934d1d9c61dd5a1abb6bf3fb213015d66e\nparent 5ed6625e4c0982512e6ec827716083e928f5406d\nauthor Jakub Zelenka <bukka@php.net> 1793550139 +0100\ncommitter Jakub Zelenka <bukka@php.net> 1793565138 +0100\n\nopenssl: Fix use-after-free in TLS session remove callback\n\nThe session remove callback reads the listener stream from the SSL_CTX\nex_data, but the context is shared with accepted connections and can\noutlive the listener. Closing the listener left a dangling pointer that\nthe callback later dereferenced. Clear it on close when it refers to the\nstream being freed.\n\nThe added test reproduces it via a TCP proxy and crashes under ASan\nwithout the fix.\n\nCloses GH-25132\n","verified_at":"2026-11-01T20:32:30Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/commits/7e86f2c443382b2f03a546b51ca065872454c087","html_url":"https://github.com/php/php-src/commit/7e86f2c443382b2f03a546b51ca065872454c087","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/commits/7e86f2c443382b2f03a546b51ca065872454c087/comments","author":{"login":"bukka","id":137594,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNzU5NA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/137594?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bukka","html_url":"https://github.com/bukka","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bukka/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bukka/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bukka/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bukka/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bukka/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bukka/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bukka/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bukka/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bukka/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"bukka","id":137594,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNzU5NA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/137594?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bukka","html_url":"https://github.com/bukka","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bukka/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bukka/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bukka/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bukka/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bukka/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bukka/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bukka/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bukka/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bukka/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"5ed6625e4c0982512e6ec827716083e928f5406d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/commits/5ed6625e4c0982512e6ec827716083e928f5406d","html_url":"https://github.com/php/php-src/commit/5ed6625e4c0982512e6ec827716083e928f5406d"}]},{"sha":"4f2bee40e04aee162d65d5c102de6b1d8ba27b51","node_id":"C_kwDOAB0LotoAKDRmMmJlZTQwZTA0YWVlMTYyZDY1ZDVjMTAyZGU2YjFkOGJhMjdiNTE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Jakub Zelenka","email":"bukka@php.net","date":"2026-11-01T18:01:26Z"},"committer":{"name":"Jakub Zelenka","email":"bukka@php.net","date":"2026-11-01T20:51:03Z"},"message":"openssl: Fix heap buffer overflow in TLS PSK callbacks\n\nThe PSK callbacks copied the user-returned identity and key into\nfixed-size buffers without checking their length. The constructor of\nOpenssl\\Psk enforces the limits, but unserialize() bypasses it, so an\noversized string overflowed the buffer. Bound each length to its buffer\nbefore copying.\n\nCloses GH-25134\n\nCo-authored-by: Tristan Madani <1075304+TristanInSec@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"8075c7ab105952ee68fc0db2776d0acaf8886ef2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/git/trees/8075c7ab105952ee68fc0db2776d0acaf8886ef2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/git/commits/4f2bee40e04aee162d65d5c102de6b1d8ba27b51","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQTCjZN1dWA+tKu3JYYcB3ncXAqd5AUCauemSgAKCRAcB3ncXAqd\n5G8/AP0Sr87gi1N+Ul3DAo/BKCPV+qWLCR4hHFUZVDwaFjtxwQD/UE3RYGDd7rIz\nuvvB8vnaSlh5gtKzD+hYJR3NgDCiZQc=\n=/y+V\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","payload":"tree 8075c7ab105952ee68fc0db2776d0acaf8886ef2\nparent 7e86f2c443382b2f03a546b51ca065872454c087\nauthor Jakub Zelenka <bukka@php.net> 1793556086 +0100\ncommitter Jakub Zelenka <bukka@php.net> 1793566263 +0100\n\nopenssl: Fix heap buffer overflow in TLS PSK callbacks\n\nThe PSK callbacks copied the user-returned identity and key into\nfixed-size buffers without checking their length. The constructor of\nOpenssl\\Psk enforces the limits, but unserialize() bypasses it, so an\noversized string overflowed the buffer. Bound each length to its buffer\nbefore copying.\n\nCloses GH-25134\n\nCo-authored-by: Tristan Madani <1075304+TristanInSec@users.noreply.github.com>\n","verified_at":"2026-11-01T20:51:39Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/commits/4f2bee40e04aee162d65d5c102de6b1d8ba27b51","html_url":"https://github.com/php/php-src/commit/4f2bee40e04aee162d65d5c102de6b1d8ba27b51","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/commits/4f2bee40e04aee162d65d5c102de6b1d8ba27b51/comments","author":{"login":"bukka","id":137594,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNzU5NA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/137594?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bukka","html_url":"https://github.com/bukka","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bukka/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bukka/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bukka/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bukka/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bukka/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bukka/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bukka/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bukka/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bukka/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"bukka","id":137594,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNzU5NA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/137594?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bukka","html_url":"https://github.com/bukka","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bukka/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bukka/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bukka/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bukka/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bukka/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bukka/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bukka/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bukka/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bukka/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"7e86f2c443382b2f03a546b51ca065872454c087","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/commits/7e86f2c443382b2f03a546b51ca065872454c087","html_url":"https://github.com/php/php-src/commit/7e86f2c443382b2f03a546b51ca065872454c087"}]},{"sha":"1e1eb7f63acb5fc96f8fbe307b1f4477e0d5948f","node_id":"C_kwDOAB0LotoAKDFlMWViN2Y2M2FjYjVmYzk2ZjhmYmUzMDdiMWY0NDc3ZTBkNTk0OGY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Lazizbek Ergashev","email":"lazerg2@gmail.com","date":"2026-11-01T21:05:18Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-11-01T21:05:18Z"},"message":"Fix GH-25086: Io\\Poll kqueue backend leaks memory on every modifyEvents() (#25087)\n\nkqueue_backend_modify() only deleted the filters that were not in the new\nevent set, so when no delete succeeded it assumed the FD had no filters\nbefore and added the full new set to filter_count. Going from Read to\nRead+Write therefore counted the already registered read filter again.\nget_suitable_max_events() returns filter_count, so every wait() grew the\nstruct kevent buffer by one entry per modify. It now deletes both filters\nfirst, which gives the real number of registered filters, and then adds\nthe requested ones. As a side effect, switching an existing watcher to\none-shot or edge-triggered now takes effect, since EV_ADD on an existing\nfilter kept its old EV_ONESHOT/EV_CLEAR flags.\n\nRe-arming a fired one-shot watcher grew the buffer the same way, because\nwait() never took the filters the kernel dropped out of filter_count. It\nnow does, including the leftover filter it deletes for read+write\none-shot watchers.\n\nCloses GH-25087.\n\nCo-authored-by: Jakub Zelenka <bukka@php.net>","tree":{"sha":"984d4a4fa4ba2d4af1d74abbd9da10cff319a727","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/git/trees/984d4a4fa4ba2d4af1d74abbd9da10cff319a727"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/git/commits/1e1eb7f63acb5fc96f8fbe307b1f4477e0d5948f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJq56mOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmCEQAA3RTg+BGlRvvoRLUKWEVSJg\nHXxqNQ7sizA6a4e0zUtnD/lzoA72sdjxl+oF73f/kpMe1oCHUW9DTMkSKVkFuxT3\nK66Nkn8QxNi1aXWbfnKnjhjtTghGTouySyb041NBBFeWATivCQtNs6lNHfnGjjQ+\nPsVSx+kJ0fYEmB65JpZOqq5vNnhNov8V8m7z0CV0MHxUqZGzcg5NZwX0/ILerPF4\nh/c7gke++6kMkm5qmTcta7eqtpVpCEjI+Pva0g41wsWDebDW1r11RT8bVu6DuFi3\nWu0Bhh2utLLuES7u6gqIFzbeXq5cDQ6qKP0m/COdeSXBamji02vD9dgcaVjulRof\nNnuILRJQ84/eMP5P+HxCjJlM1S3Mfa+R0oJ9M8Rt1I3eVNCBPagIRHpgP9YxDa6z\nGOPVAmrUiNME6UQTx19lnYAVGeEZYGJ02WpmCRWjzyU0RdV58/79dFSXXevvfdqa\n/GM2KOfFyHo1Te9PqLMKXAtkvydnMLL28enHwzgTNZy/nCN81J4bOf6nhcG//leF\n7O+/dl3GVyTec0VvkYYZXDpFFnsr6UcYkUYf7Z1BbxFKEXw7vhMDN3E4DUSpd6sj\nQMu4o+RLGAgjrHy5jdu//qIzz1f/WAvFQU2fu9Z+MDcAUTwy9Vsn41bGlAfF3F35\nXD+FBkoZyWpDL2kq3ds/\n=AVM5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 984d4a4fa4ba2d4af1d74abbd9da10cff319a727\nparent 4f2bee40e04aee162d65d5c102de6b1d8ba27b51\nauthor Lazizbek Ergashev <lazerg2@gmail.com> 1793567118 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1793567118 +0100\n\nFix GH-25086: Io\\Poll kqueue backend leaks memory on every modifyEvents() (#25087)\n\nkqueue_backend_modify() only deleted the filters that were not in the new\nevent set, so when no delete succeeded it assumed the FD had no filters\nbefore and added the full new set to filter_count. Going from Read to\nRead+Write therefore counted the already registered read filter again.\nget_suitable_max_events() returns filter_count, so every wait() grew the\nstruct kevent buffer by one entry per modify. It now deletes both filters\nfirst, which gives the real number of registered filters, and then adds\nthe requested ones. As a side effect, switching an existing watcher to\none-shot or edge-triggered now takes effect, since EV_ADD on an existing\nfilter kept its old EV_ONESHOT/EV_CLEAR flags.\n\nRe-arming a fired one-shot watcher grew the buffer the same way, because\nwait() never took the filters the kernel dropped out of filter_count. It\nnow does, including the leftover filter it deletes for read+write\none-shot watchers.\n\nCloses GH-25087.\n\nCo-authored-by: Jakub Zelenka <bukka@php.net>","verified_at":"2026-11-01T21:05:18Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/commits/1e1eb7f63acb5fc96f8fbe307b1f4477e0d5948f","html_url":"https://github.com/php/php-src/commit/1e1eb7f63acb5fc96f8fbe307b1f4477e0d5948f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/commits/1e1eb7f63acb5fc96f8fbe307b1f4477e0d5948f/comments","author":{"login":"lazerg","id":20501725,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNTAxNzI1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20501725?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazerg","html_url":"https://github.com/lazerg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazerg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazerg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazerg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazerg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazerg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazerg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazerg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazerg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazerg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4f2bee40e04aee162d65d5c102de6b1d8ba27b51","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/commits/4f2bee40e04aee162d65d5c102de6b1d8ba27b51","html_url":"https://github.com/php/php-src/commit/4f2bee40e04aee162d65d5c102de6b1d8ba27b51"}]},{"sha":"f2fbe476d3bffd794864262403abc482cccf9de6","node_id":"C_kwDOAB0LotoAKGYyZmJlNDc2ZDNiZmZkNzk0ODY0MjYyNDAzYWJjNDgyY2NjZjlkZTY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Nicolas Grekas","email":"nicolas.grekas@gmail.com","date":"2026-11-01T19:07:39Z"},"committer":{"name":"Jakub Zelenka","email":"bukka@php.net","date":"2026-11-01T21:09:39Z"},"message":"Fix the WSAPoll backend of Io\\Poll accepting handles that are not sockets\n\nWSAPoll() can only poll sockets, but the backend accepted any fd. A file\nor a pipe such as STDOUT was then dropped by wait() without being\nreported. Adding such a handle now fails with ERR_NOSUPPORT, as epoll\ndoes for regular files.\n\nCloses GH-25135.","tree":{"sha":"7458a8e9ee2174c9d79711a63c650131a0b0beae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/git/trees/7458a8e9ee2174c9d79711a63c650131a0b0beae"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/git/commits/f2fbe476d3bffd794864262403abc482cccf9de6","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQTCjZN1dWA+tKu3JYYcB3ncXAqd5AUCaueqkwAKCRAcB3ncXAqd\n5Nj0AP9qxycYo/49a3r4jsyH1/ryBFlMunSZIaGkH419ngNYBwEA3NnzFOQuVNdZ\njoAL8jBMhHIxAX3SOFKsCNpcMObsGQE=\n=iQ9I\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","payload":"tree 7458a8e9ee2174c9d79711a63c650131a0b0beae\nparent 1e1eb7f63acb5fc96f8fbe307b1f4477e0d5948f\nauthor Nicolas Grekas <nicolas.grekas@gmail.com> 1793560059 +0100\ncommitter Jakub Zelenka <bukka@php.net> 1793567379 +0100\n\nFix the WSAPoll backend of Io\\Poll accepting handles that are not sockets\n\nWSAPoll() can only poll sockets, but the backend accepted any fd. A file\nor a pipe such as STDOUT was then dropped by wait() without being\nreported. Adding such a handle now fails with ERR_NOSUPPORT, as epoll\ndoes for regular files.\n\nCloses GH-25135.\n","verified_at":"2026-11-01T21:10:17Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/commits/f2fbe476d3bffd794864262403abc482cccf9de6","html_url":"https://github.com/php/php-src/commit/f2fbe476d3bffd794864262403abc482cccf9de6","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/commits/f2fbe476d3bffd794864262403abc482cccf9de6/comments","author":{"login":"nicolas-grekas","id":243674,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MzY3NA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/243674?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolas-grekas","html_url":"https://github.com/nicolas-grekas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolas-grekas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolas-grekas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolas-grekas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolas-grekas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolas-grekas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolas-grekas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolas-grekas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolas-grekas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicolas-grekas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"bukka","id":137594,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNzU5NA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/137594?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bukka","html_url":"https://github.com/bukka","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bukka/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bukka/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bukka/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bukka/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bukka/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bukka/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bukka/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bukka/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bukka/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"1e1eb7f63acb5fc96f8fbe307b1f4477e0d5948f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/commits/1e1eb7f63acb5fc96f8fbe307b1f4477e0d5948f","html_url":"https://github.com/php/php-src/commit/1e1eb7f63acb5fc96f8fbe307b1f4477e0d5948f"}]},{"sha":"2ff2085fa4583244fc6b3ff3596707453dca1b3c","node_id":"C_kwDOAB0LotoAKDJmZjIwODVmYTQ1ODMyNDRmYzZiM2ZmMzU5NjcwNzQ1M2RjYTFiM2M","commit":{"author":{"name":"lazerg","email":"lazerg2@gmail.com","date":"2026-11-02T06:18:01Z"},"committer":{"name":"Weilin Du","email":"weilindu@php.net","date":"2026-11-02T06:18:17Z"},"message":"Fix GH-25093: Phar::webPhar() redirect reads past the request URI (#25102)\n\nOn non-CGI SAPIs, a direct request advances a pointer into the request\nURI by the length of the full phar path. This can read past the URI,\nincluding when a rewrite callback returns '/'.\n\nAdvance by the basename length, as the target path construction does.\nAdd a regression test and a NEWS entry.\n\nCloses #25102","tree":{"sha":"f6d338de6d8af6889367893ace50349027ac0d6b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/git/trees/f6d338de6d8af6889367893ace50349027ac0d6b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/git/commits/2ff2085fa4583244fc6b3ff3596707453dca1b3c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQJPBAABCAA5FiEEaDXx4YiBo+JEKqlm6j2Y1d107h8FAmroKykbFIAAAAAABAAO\nbWFudTIsMi41KzEuMTIsMiwxAAoJEOo9mNXddO4fwXsP/2wBYbA3+d1f3oUN28Wr\nIUptyKxScOlPnPUWKz+bJfg/F/hrS06P1V2J5Z0DKJPcxNaHA2p8vlE+v7hfOc1K\nLGaEII2j8s2GJjVSvSXZcB1DrswuCYieINPl6SWePFuAOxrqA9FEv1UM26gKPVzU\nORszg/QRdKTVeFD0wgJ6aYIgNekVbkpS4d/qBT1A4tJnzOSrlN5sTWOtSHenlFP/\n1ZDtqxeVFNiBuYPGsnl1UoL/cDPbodr0nPyPwp3OPWW2qxcsEiAclRBylHt7KJ7c\nYNBZeGdfgxsYBo94XfyZtMWWeVJmpMRjrZ3L4cx22C98b2ofbxqwbEMeHEtKVfEC\nxdDaEFnMCgzfGE9uUEMm2YCI3jYfNodCazLXacs9vQdq6ABG7NxoMVoeH3Zbk4bj\nP4VNTnCd1dl08+NP8rzMnS4ySqQ7/KbqmgOQh8q4asCNHL/ZioAhAA4rh1Kjfh4L\nIdOQW2gL1S9hBULiWbmDfZUkCwoN0yiibf661EB7v4rsHCiEDqnWnlXxoRRngijR\n5MSmDpwWKZ8H+IqyRG4CYPRMZVfSMgP8IpImgMbfHURXIMDuIHB2JOcLiDKRDy+z\n9rM8rZbkX8TQ6OCXhA8MM5jHdw2PsobstHZNwaWNFDKkzx8Kdp3JENWGGcZZJS2A\nn2FOyLprsNkE752W5o9W2CEe\n=mjMC\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","payload":"tree f6d338de6d8af6889367893ace50349027ac0d6b\nparent 7091e5b029f24b7d091dee73432c2cca260a90fe\nauthor lazerg <lazerg2@gmail.com> 1793600281 +0800\ncommitter Weilin Du <weilindu@php.net> 1793600297 +0800\n\nFix GH-25093: Phar::webPhar() redirect reads past the request URI (#25102)\n\nOn non-CGI SAPIs, a direct request advances a pointer into the request\nURI by the length of the full phar path. This can read past the URI,\nincluding when a rewrite callback returns '/'.\n\nAdvance by the basename length, as the target path construction does.\nAdd a regression test and a NEWS entry.\n\nCloses #25102\n","verified_at":"2026-11-02T06:29:49Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/commits/2ff2085fa4583244fc6b3ff3596707453dca1b3c","html_url":"https://github.com/php/php-src/commit/2ff2085fa4583244fc6b3ff3596707453dca1b3c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/commits/2ff2085fa4583244fc6b3ff3596707453dca1b3c/comments","author":{"login":"lazerg","id":20501725,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNTAxNzI1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20501725?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazerg","html_url":"https://github.com/lazerg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazerg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazerg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazerg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazerg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazerg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazerg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazerg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazerg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lazerg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"LamentXU123","id":108666168,"node_id":"U_kgDOBnodOA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/108666168?v=4","gra