"2026-11-02T18:19:14Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/commits/9bcb8487a7adf5a0d0a9852bac0bb78f69838a60","html_url":"https://github.com/php/php-src/commit/9bcb8487a7adf5a0d0a9852bac0bb78f69838a60","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/commits/9bcb8487a7adf5a0d0a9852bac0bb78f69838a60/comments","author":{"login":"shivammathur","id":1571086,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1NzEwODY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1571086?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shivammathur","html_url":"https://github.com/shivammathur","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shivammathur/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shivammathur/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shivammathur/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shivammathur/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shivammathur/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shivammathur/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shivammathur/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shivammathur/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shivammathur/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"shivammathur","id":1571086,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1NzEwODY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1571086?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shivammathur","html_url":"https://github.com/shivammathur","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shivammathur/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shivammathur/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shivammathur/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shivammathur/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shivammathur/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shivammathur/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shivammathur/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shivammathur/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shivammathur/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"57978902becd3995db1acba0e9e3f825d0b4f2e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/commits/57978902becd3995db1acba0e9e3f825d0b4f2e3","html_url":"https://github.com/php/php-src/commit/57978902becd3995db1acba0e9e3f825d0b4f2e3"},{"sha":"c6f843008a47e38e7c2efda99e1f0c44771a2db0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/commits/c6f843008a47e38e7c2efda99e1f0c44771a2db0","html_url":"https://github.com/php/php-src/commit/c6f843008a47e38e7c2efda99e1f0c44771a2db0"}]},{"sha":"07fc1f9d2f8da87519fcf955cef9ce23daf3944e","node_id":"C_kwDOAB0LotoAKDA3ZmMxZjlkMmY4ZGE4NzUxOWZjZjk1NWNlZjljZTIzZGFmMzk0NGU","commit":{"author":{"name":"C. Scott Ananian","email":"cscott@cscott.net","date":"2026-10-21T04:12:14Z"},"committer":{"name":"David Carlier","email":"devnexen@gmail.com","date":"2026-11-02T18:32:45Z"},"message":"Fix GH-24480: finally block running twice when a VM interrupt throws in FAST_RET\n\n\"return\" inside a try block with a finally block compiles to FAST_CALL,\nwhich runs the finally block, followed by the RETURN. Both are inside the\ntry range. FAST_RET jumps back to the RETURN with ZEND_VM_JMP_EX(), which\nchecks for interrupts after setting opline to the RETURN. If an interrupt\nis pending at that point and the interrupt function throws (an async\npcntl signal handler, a request timeout from Excimer, ...), the exception\nis attributed to the RETURN, i.e. to the try block, so the finally block\nruns a second time and the pending return value leaks. This is the\ncommon case when the interrupt arrives during a user function called\nfrom the finally block, since returning from a user function does not\ncheck for interrupts in the hybrid VM.\n\nThe CALL VM checks for interrupts after every return from a user\nfunction instead, with opline at the FAST_RET that follows the call.\nThere the exception is attributed to FAST_RET, which is finally_end and\nso counted as outside the try/finally: the pending return value, and any\nexception the finally block was delaying, leak.\n\nHandle interrupts in FAST_RET before the jump, while opline is still\nFAST_RET, and treat an exception thrown at FAST_RET as thrown inside its\nfinally block in ZEND_HANDLE_EXCEPTION and\nzend_dispatch_try_catch_finally_helper. This discards the pending return\nvalue and chains a delayed exception, as for any other exception thrown\nin the finally block, in both VM kinds.\n\nAdd zend_test.observer.set_vm_interrupt_on_end, which sets a pending\ninterrupt that throws as an observed function returns, to test this\ndeterministically.\n\nCloses GH-24480\nClose GH-24486","tree":{"sha":"07258f244693d416c673321bf2ec719169168a5a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/git/trees/07258f244693d416c673321bf2ec719169168a5a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/git/commits/07fc1f9d2f8da87519fcf955cef9ce23daf3944e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQGzBAABCgAdFiEE2uPA2CxuntXfTtGCHhkLTi6CjtcFAmro100ACgkQHhkLTi6C\njtcNlQv+LXy6Ht9kTcvfTeBirsxPiNiNe/B4CMI6ry2UQt2S+z7/jRXs3j2aWKrb\nPAAcWcHOvyX/QMdwEaaYVIusGINtpO5nMLuNYFvHgxgvSRIhxBldmwE8eX5qdH8Q\nTpdks/i7FYi2vf1CF/7U501vPzYK5zy+v82niP+QP0CM/f4Xs7BObWelYV+VIVBI\n/7WYdnRLzI9X1bOsD6pN1hgTpy73PYjpRa1wAjoXO2ECOD5shj49O+A/J9+Llwzi\nptZtgBVoyn5SAy/NyuvWYQ5gt4uMO3hmZgka51fZ+EPVPF7WOExiKlZSngznxu1c\nMdB26dfyLJgBl4RDZ+NmGGLoCVZyJo7Q2NT9Hi91UBr5XRglmcl1nUoNtLEJ7FYS\nvRTeayzwarZ7SG0LIG5Aqb+rrBO/KmGBl6yQfRyrs0hbKfU3XGRmZmzr2Y6V9J0x\ngdnHBTrTcVmiJDq9Jd8U4ZXWXCQCmOAyLpQ3PkPjKfGjL/jmjPdrbk7Ecp2MBJOX\nrdiDvf1u\n=brxy\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","payload":"tree 07258f244693d416c673321bf2ec719169168a5a\nparent 4dece7547190100457b4f62ef0a4e68c2cf826cc\nauthor C. Scott Ananian <cscott@cscott.net> 1792555934 -0400\ncommitter David Carlier <devnexen@gmail.com> 1793644365 +0000\n\nFix GH-24480: finally block running twice when a VM interrupt throws in FAST_RET\n\n\"return\" inside a try block with a finally block compiles to FAST_CALL,\nwhich runs the finally block, followed by the RETURN. Both are inside the\ntry range. FAST_RET jumps back to the RETURN with ZEND_VM_JMP_EX(), which\nchecks for interrupts after setting opline to the RETURN. If an interrupt\nis pending at that point and the interrupt function throws (an async\npcntl signal handler, a request timeout from Excimer, ...), the exception\nis attributed to the RETURN, i.e. to the try block, so the finally block\nruns a second time and the pending return value leaks. This is the\ncommon case when the interrupt arrives during a user function called\nfrom the finally block, since returning from a user function does not\ncheck for interrupts in the hybrid VM.\n\nThe CALL VM checks for interrupts after every return from a user\nfunction instead, with opline at the FAST_RET that follows the call.\nThere the exception is attributed to FAST_RET, which is finally_end and\nso counted as outside the try/finally: the pending return value, and any\nexception the finally block was delaying, leak.\n\nHandle interrupts in FAST_RET before the jump, while opline is still\nFAST_RET, and treat an exception thrown at FAST_RET as thrown inside its\nfinally block in ZEND_HANDLE_EXCEPTION and\nzend_dispatch_try_catch_finally_helper. This discards the pending return\nvalue and chains a delayed exception, as for any other exception thrown\nin the finally block, in both VM kinds.\n\nAdd zend_test.observer.set_vm_interrupt_on_end, which sets a pending\ninterrupt that throws as an observed function returns, to test this\ndeterministically.\n\nCloses GH-24480\nClose GH-24486\n","verified_at":"2026-11-02T18:35:41Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/p